{
  "_about": [
    "§74's two halves, pinned in one file. Every entry here is either an answer this API actually produces",
    "(producer.kind = handler | door, checked against the shipped tree by",
    "apps/api/tests/test_error_answer_shape.py) or a payload a client can still meet from somewhere else",
    "(producer.kind = reader-tolerance, with the reason stated in `why`).",
    "",
    "The web gate that reads this file is apps/web/scripts/qa-error-shape.mjs: it loads the shipped",
    "apps/web/lib/api.ts, feeds each body through browserFetch -> readError -> normalizeError with fetch",
    "stubbed, and asserts what survives the trip. What the API puts at detail.code must arrive as error.code;",
    "before §74 the handlers answered {error: {…}} and the reader handed the user 'Request failed' instead of",
    "a sentence the API had already written."
  ],
  "entries": [
    {
      "name": "handler-422-validation-error",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "handler",
        "site": "app/core/errors.py::_validation",
        "code": "validation_error",
        "message": "Request validation failed"
      },
      "status": 422,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "validation_error",
            "message": "Request validation failed",
            "details": [
              {
                "type": "string_too_short",
                "loc": [
                  "body",
                  "display_name"
                ],
                "msg": "String should have at least 2 characters"
              },
              {
                "type": "too_short",
                "loc": [
                  "body",
                  "password"
                ],
                "msg": "String should have at least 8 characters"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "handler-409-integrity-error",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "handler",
        "site": "app/core/errors.py::_integrity",
        "code": "conflict",
        "message": "That record conflicts with existing data"
      },
      "status": 409,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "conflict",
            "message": "That record conflicts with existing data"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "handler-500-unhandled",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "handler",
        "site": "app/core/errors.py::_unhandled",
        "code": "internal_error",
        "message": "Unexpected server error"
      },
      "status": 500,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "internal_error",
            "message": "Unexpected server error"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "door-422-careers-no-objectives",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "door",
        "module": "app/api/v1/careers.py",
        "code": "no_objectives",
        "message": "a career needs at least one objective to be judged by"
      },
      "status": 422,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "no_objectives",
            "message": "a career needs at least one objective to be judged by",
            "see": [
              "fitness",
              "tactics",
              "results",
              "finance",
              "development"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "door-409-coach-no-player",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "door",
        "module": "app/api/v1/coach.py",
        "code": "no_player",
        "message": "Create your player profile first"
      },
      "status": 409,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "no_player",
            "message": "Create your player profile first"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "door-404-boards-link-gone",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "door",
        "module": "app/api/v1/boards.py",
        "code": "not_found",
        "message": "This link no longer points at a board"
      },
      "status": 404,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": {
            "code": "not_found",
            "message": "This link no longer points at a board"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "tolerance-plain-string-detail",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "reader-tolerance",
        "why": "FastAPI's own default for an unanswered route answers detail as a string; the sentence must still reach the page."
      },
      "status": 404,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": "Not Found"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": "error",
        "message": "Not Found"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "tolerance-array-detail",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "reader-tolerance",
        "why": "An uninstalled 422 answers detail as a list; the reader must not call that list an object and print [object Object]."
      },
      "status": 422,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "detail": [
            {
              "loc": [
                "body",
                "email"
              ],
              "msg": "field required",
              "type": "missing"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": "error",
        "message": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "tolerance-not-json-body",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "reader-tolerance",
        "why": "A proxy or a crashed worker can answer HTML on a JSON endpoint; readError must still yield a sentence."
      },
      "status": 502,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "text/html",
        "text": "<html><body>502 Bad Gateway</body></html>"
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": "error",
        "message": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "tolerance-flat-refusal",
      "producer": {
        "kind": "reader-tolerance",
        "why": "lib/api.ts keeps the pre-§74 flat spelling readable on purpose: a refusal that arrives with its figures beside the sentence must not lose them."
      },
      "status": 402,
      "body": {
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "json": {
          "code": "budget_exceeded",
          "message": "The wage bill would exceed the budget",
          "remaining": 120000,
          "requested": 300000
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "code": "budget_exceeded",
        "message": "The wage bill would exceed the budget",
        "figure_keys": [
          "remaining",
          "requested"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
